## 1. Objective
This entry establishes a theoretical framework for **Cross-Modal Data Transduction**. The goal is to identify "neural backdoors"—non-standard sensory pathways (olfactory, gustatory, and visceral/interoceptive)—that possess higher plasticity and lower cognitive filtering than the primary visual and auditory channels. By mapping digital state-changes to these "phantom" senses, we can bypass the "uncanny valley" of haptics and create a somatic bond that feels innate rather than simulated.

